$y=x+5$.
Exchange $x$ and $y$.
$\begin{aligned}x&=y+5\\y&=x-5\\f^{-1}(x)&=x-5\end{aligned}$
Both lines have gradient $1$, with different intercepts $5$ and $-5$. They are parallel, so there are no intersections.
